### 🎯 Key Engineering Requirements for Maximum Efficiency

| Metric | Target Standard | Engineering Implementation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Go Agent CPU Usage** | **< 1% Idle**, **< 5% Active** | OS-native kernel event notifications (`fsnotify` / `ReadDirectoryChangesW`) instead of recursive polling loops. |
| **Go Agent RAM Footprint** | **5 MB – 15 MB** | Compiled Go native binary with zero heavy runtime overhead. |
| **Node.js Server RAM** | **30 MB – 50 MB** | Lightweight Express + WebSocket process managing background tasks. |
| **Heartbeat Frequency** | **30 Seconds** | Timely check-ins keeping employee status **Online** without overloading database IOPS. |
| **Log Transmission** | **5-Second Batching** | Buffer local events in memory and insert in bulk batches of 50 to prevent hitting Supabase HTTP 429 rate limits. |
| **RLS Security** | **Service Role Bypass for System Logs** | `server.js` uses `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` for heartbeat & ACK writes, ensuring non-blocking system operations. |

